Version pin was wrong (see the comment above `version=` in the recipe
itself) - fixed to the real latest release tag and its "-src" asset. That
part is confirmed working: source now fetches, extracts, and compiles
well into the dependency graph.

Blocked past that on a real upstream compatibility gap, not an Arctic
packaging bug: `openssl-sys` 0.9.99 (pulled in transitively) refuses to
build against anything newer than LibreSSL 3.8.1 -

  This crate is only compatible with OpenSSL (version 1.0.1 through
  1.1.1, or 3), or LibreSSL 2.5 through 3.8.1, but a different version of
  OpenSSL was found.

Arctic ships LibreSSL 4.2.0. Forcing a different openssl-sys version
would need an actual Cargo.lock edit (the build runs --locked, same
reasoning as every other Rust recipe here), which risks cascading into
every other crate that also pins around openssl-sys's version - not
attempted this pass. A newer wezterm release, or an openssl-sys bump
upstream, may already have moved past this; worth re-checking before
patching Cargo.lock by hand.
